WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.696 --> 00:00:10.270
- Okay, welcome everyone

00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:13.020
and thank you for joining us this evening

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:17.337
for our presentation and
discussion of an academic paper,

00:00:17.337 --> 00:00:21.110
"Safe Seats and Female
(Under)Representation

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:25.650
in the U.S. Congress" by Akhil Rajan,

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:27.780
Alexander Kustov,

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:29.280
Maikol Cerda,

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:30.590
Frances Rosenbluth

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:31.973
and Ian Shapiro.

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:36.400
This event is part of a series of events

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:41.400
that ISPS, the Institution
for Social and Policy Studies,

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:46.300
is holding this year called ISPS Democracy

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:49.360
and these events bring
together experts from Yale

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:52.870
and beyond to shed light
on key questions concerning

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:56.173
American politics,
governance and democracy.

00:00:58.105 --> 00:01:01.470
The next event in this
ISPS Democracy series

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:06.140
will be Tuesday, April 13th, at 4:00 pm,

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:07.610
our regular time is seven,

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:09.590
but this is at 4:00 pm,

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:12.310
rethinking political representation

00:01:12.310 --> 00:01:14.300
where we'll have a number of experts

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:18.090
on novel ways of holding elections

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:21.890
and engaging in legislative deliberations.

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:26.310
Before I continue on to
discuss tonight's event

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:30.030
I wanna make sure to thank
the organizers of this event

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:35.030
Pam Greene, Pam Lamonaca,
Tory Bilski and Limor Peer.

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:39.890
So here are the logistics
for tonight's event,

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:41.900
we'll have the authors present their work

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:43.820
