00:02:47.808 --> 00:02:50.800
With that, let me introduce
tonight's participants.

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:53.680
First, the presenting authors,

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:56.260
Ian Shapiro is the Sterling Professor

00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:59.380
of political science at Yale University.

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:01.880
He served as chair of political science

00:03:04.411 --> 00:03:05.910
from 1999,

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:08.240
no that's, I think that's,

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:09.950
I bet longer than that.

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:11.470
You served as chair of political science

00:03:11.470 --> 00:03:12.740
for a number of years,

00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:15.370
very successful and wonderful years,

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:18.190
and you also served as the director

00:03:18.190 --> 00:03:21.320
of the MacMillan Center for
International and Area Studies

00:03:22.532 --> 00:03:25.810
from 2004 to 2019

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:27.500
and as a fellow of the American Academy

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:28.580
of Arts and Sciences,

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:31.120
the American Philosophical Society

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:33.760
