And our panelist authors,

01:10:09.150 --> 01:10:12.510
is there anything else you'd
like to say before we conclude?

01:10:12.510 --> 01:10:14.360
- No, thank you for having us.

01:10:14.360 --> 01:10:15.193
- It's a pleasure,

01:10:15.193 --> 01:10:16.253
absolute pleasure.

01:10:17.230 --> 01:10:20.830
Well, let me say, Frances and Jonathan,

01:10:20.830 --> 01:10:24.764
you are welcome at any time
you wanna drop in here to Yale

01:10:24.764 --> 01:10:28.863
and it reminds us just how
wonderful our colleagues are

01:10:28.863 --> 01:10:31.309
out there in the big world

01:10:31.309 --> 01:10:35.560
and thank you for such
thoughtful contributions

01:10:35.560 --> 01:10:37.140
to the discussion.

01:10:37.140 --> 01:10:40.920
And, of course, thank you
to the authors for this,

01:10:40.920 --> 01:10:44.110
you know, illuminating
and stimulating paper.

01:10:44.110 --> 01:10:46.190
This is a dimension to safe seats

01:10:46.190 --> 01:10:48.660
that I think no one contemplated

01:10:48.660 --> 01:10:51.032
and it will definitely
affect the way I look

01:10:51.032 --> 01:10:55.560
at the patterns of congressional
competition moving forward.

01:10:55.560 --> 01:10:57.293
So again, thank you all so much.

